---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: Static Site Spec
description: The canonical architecture and conventions for building modern static websites.
bodyClass: is-blueprint
---
{# Each section is a chapter: when it reaches mid-screen it announces the pose
   it wants the drawing in. The words all live here; the drawing only repeats
   a few of them as labels. #}
{% macro chapter(id) -%}
{%- for c in blueprint.chapters %}{% if c.id == id -%}
data-controller="chapter" data-chapter-scene-value="blueprint" data-chapter-look-value="{{ c | dump }}"
{%- endif %}{% endfor -%}
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro summary(url) -%}
{%- for p in collections.all %}{% if p.url == url %}{{ p.data.description }}{% endif %}{% endfor -%}
{%- endmacro %}

<div class="blueprint" data-controller="blueprint">
  <canvas class="sheet" data-blueprint-target="canvas" aria-hidden="true"></canvas>
  <div class="sheet-fallback" hidden data-blueprint-target="fallback"></div>

  <section class="plate plate--cover" {{ chapter("cover") }}>
    <p class="plate-kicker">Sheet 1 of 1 <span aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span> Revision {{ site.version }}</p>
    <h1 class="plate-title">Static Site Spec</h1>
    <p class="plate-lede">The canonical architecture and conventions for building static websites with Eleventy, Tailwind CSS 4, and Stimulus. Prescriptive, so every site built to it has the same body plan.</p>
    <div class="plate-actions">
      <a class="plate-button plate-button--solid" href="{{ '/getting-started/' | url }}">Get started</a>
      <a class="plate-button" href="{{ site.github }}">View on GitHub</a>
    </div>
    <p class="plate-hint">Scroll to take it apart</p>
  </section>

  <section class="plate" aria-labelledby="stack-title" {{ chapter("stack") }}>
    <p class="plate-kicker">Detail A <span aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span> The stack</p>
    <h2 class="plate-heading" id="stack-title">Three layers, one job each</h2>
    <dl class="plate-parts">
      <div><dt>Eleventy 3.1</dt><dd>Builds HTML from Nunjucks templates and data files.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Tailwind CSS 4.1</dt><dd>Styles from design tokens, configured in one CSS file.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Stimulus 3.2</dt><dd>Behavior attached to the HTML that is already there.</dd></div>
    </dl>
    <a class="plate-link" href="{{ '/stack/' | url }}">Why these three</a>
  </section>

  <section class="plate" aria-labelledby="structure-title" {{ chapter("structure") }}>
    <p class="plate-kicker">Detail B <span aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span> Structure</p>
    <h2 class="plate-heading" id="structure-title">A place for everything</h2>
    <p>Every site has the same tree: data in <code>_data/</code>, layouts and partials in <code>_includes/</code>, styles and controllers in <code>assets/</code>, and pages at the top. Know one site built to the spec and you know where everything is in the next.</p>
    <a class="plate-link" href="{{ '/structure/' | url }}">The directory structure</a>
  </section>

  <section class="plate" aria-labelledby="build-title" {{ chapter("build") }}>
    <p class="plate-kicker">Detail C <span aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span> Build</p>
    <h2 class="plate-heading" id="build-title">One command builds it</h2>
    <p><code>npm run build</code> reads the data, renders the templates, compiles Tailwind in a single before hook, and writes <code>dist/</code>. GitHub Actions runs the same command on every push and publishes the result.</p>
    <a class="plate-link" href="{{ '/deployment/' | url }}">Build and deploy</a>
  </section>

  <section class="plate" aria-labelledby="controllers-title" {{ chapter("controllers") }}>
    <p class="plate-kicker">Detail D <span aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span> Controllers</p>
    <h2 class="plate-heading" id="controllers-title">Behavior, wired in the markup</h2>
    <p>Small Stimulus controllers, attached with data attributes, each doing one thing. Menus, scroll reveals, forms, search, and copy buttons, ready to drop in.</p>
    <ul class="plate-controllers">
      {%- for item in sections.controllers %}{% if item.title != "Overview" %}
      <li><a href="{{ item.url | url }}"><code>{{ item.title }}</code></a></li>
      {%- endif %}{% endfor %}
    </ul>
    <a class="plate-link" href="{{ '/controllers/' | url }}">All controllers</a>
  </section>

  <section class="plate" aria-labelledby="scene-title" {{ chapter("scene-sites") }}>
    <p class="plate-kicker">Detail E <span aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span> New in {{ site.version }}</p>
    <h2 class="plate-heading" id="scene-title">This page is a scene site</h2>
    <p>Each section you scroll past is a chapter that announces the pose it wants. One controller owns the loop and hands the time to small modules that know nothing about the page. The drawing behind these words is the system they describe.</p>
    <a class="plate-link" href="{{ '/scene-sites/' | url }}">Scene sites</a>
  </section>

  <section class="plate plate--title" aria-labelledby="title-block-title" {{ chapter("title-block") }}>
    <div class="title-block">
      <h2 class="title-block-name" id="title-block-title">Static Site Specification</h2>
      <dl class="title-block-cells">
        <div><dt>Revision</dt><dd>{{ site.version }}</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Date</dt><dd>{{ site.released }}</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Drawn</dt><dd>{{ site.author }}</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Sheet</dt><dd>1 of 1</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </div>

    <h3 class="plate-subhead">Contents</h3>
    <ul class="plate-contents">
      {%- for item in sections.main.concat(sections.reference) %}
      <li><a href="{{ item.url | url }}"><strong>{{ item.title }}</strong><span>{{ summary(item.url) }}</span></a></li>
      {%- endfor %}
    </ul>

    <h3 class="plate-subhead">Built to the spec</h3>
    <ul class="plate-examples">
      <li><a href="https://dannycaruso.link"><strong>Danny Caruso</strong><span>Actor, a scene site run by lighting cues &middot; v1.7</span></a></li>
      <li><a href="https://vetmgmedia.com"><strong>VetMGMedia</strong><span>Contractor financing sites &middot; v1.6</span></a></li>
      <li><a href="https://lytle-landscape.com"><strong>Lytle Landscape</strong><span>Landscape design &middot; v1.5</span></a></li>
      <li><a href="https://engineers-manual.com"><strong>Engineer's Manual</strong><span>Technical reference &middot; v1.4</span></a></li>
      <li><a href="https://thedbtresource.com"><strong>The DBT Resource</strong><span>Educational resource &middot; v1.3</span></a></li>
      <li><a href="https://tommy2118.github.io/nomad-theater-company"><strong>Nomad Theater Company</strong><span>Theater company &middot; v1.2</span></a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</div>
